PROXY protection. This vulnerability is due to an incomplete for CVE-2025-62718, This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-24\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42043>CVE-2026-42043</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.661%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>7.2</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Changed\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: Low\n  - Integrity Impact: Low\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-pmwg-cvhr-8vh7\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-pmwg-cvhr-8vh7</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-24</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.1</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/high_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2025-62718</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/http.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.0 and 0.31.0, Axios does not correctly handle hostname normalization when checking NO_PROXY rules. Requests to loopback addresses like localhost. (with a trailing dot) or [::1] (IPv6 literal) skip NO_PROXY matching and go through the configured proxy. This goes against what developers expect and lets attackers force requests through a proxy, even if NO_PROXY is set up to protect loopback or internal services. This issue leads to the possibility of proxy bypass and SSRF vulnerabilities allowing attackers to reach sensitive loopback or internal services despite the configured protections. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.0 and 0.31.0.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-09\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2025-62718>CVE-2025-62718</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 1.186%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>7.2</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Changed\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: Low\n  - Integrity Impact: Low\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-3p68-rc4w-qgx5\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-3p68-rc4w-qgx5</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-09</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.0</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-42038</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/utils.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, he fix for no_proxy hostname normalization bypass is incomplete. When no_proxy=localhost is set, requests to 127.0.0.1 and [::1] still route through the proxy instead of bypassing it. The shouldBypassProxy() function does pure string matching — it does not resolve IP aliases or loopback equivalents. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-24\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42038>CVE-2026-42038</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.301%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>6.8</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: High\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Changed\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-m7pr-hjqh-92cm\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-m7pr-hjqh-92cm</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-24</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.1</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2024-28849</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Libraries - <b>follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz</b>, <b>follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz</b>\n<p>\n\n\n### <b>follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz</b>\n\n<p>HTTP and HTTPS modules that follow redirects.</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /achilles-frontend/package.json,/baak-vizualization/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - axios-0.21.4.tgz (Root Library)\n    - :x: **follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n\n\n### <b>follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz</b>\n\n<p>HTTP and HTTPS modules that follow redirects.</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - axios-0.21.4.tgz (Root Library)\n    - :x: **follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n\n\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/http.js (Extension)\n      -> ❌ follow-redirects-1.15.0/index.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nfollow-redirects is an open source, drop-in replacement for Node's \"http\" and \"https\" modules that automatically follows redirects. In affected versions follow-redirects only clears authorization header during cross-domain redirect, but keep the proxy-authentication header which contains credentials too. This vulnerability may lead to credentials leak, but has been addressed in version 1.15.6. Users are advised to upgrade. There are no known workarounds for this vulnerability.\n Mend Note: The description of this vulnerability differs from MITRE. \n\n<p>Publish Date: 2024-03-14\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2024-28849>CVE-2024-28849</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 1.044%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>6.5</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: Low\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/security/advisories/GHSA-cxjh-pqwp-8mfp\">https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/security/advisories/GHSA-cxjh-pqwp-8mfp</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2024-03-14</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution (follow-redirects): 1.15.6</p>\n<p>Direct dependency fix Resolution (axios): 0.22.0</p><p>Fix Resolution (follow-redirects): 1.15.6</p>\n<p>Direct dependency fix Resolution (axios): 0.22.0</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2023-45857</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/http.js (Extension)\n      -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/core/buildFullPath.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAn issue discovered in Axios 1.5.1 inadvertently reveals the confidential XSRF-TOKEN stored in cookies by including it in the HTTP header X-XSRF-TOKEN for every request made to any host allowing attackers to view sensitive information.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2023-11-08\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2023-45857>CVE-2023-45857</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.556%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>6.5</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: Required\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: High\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wf5p-g6vw-rhxx\">https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wf5p-g6vw-rhxx</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2023-11-08</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.28.0</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-39865</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/http.js (Extension)\n      -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/core/buildFullPath.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Starting in version 1.13.0 and prior to 1.13.2, Axios HTTP/2 session cleanup logic contains a state corruption bug that allows a malicious server to crash the client process through concurrent session closures. The vulnerability exists in the Http2Sessions.getSession() method in lib/adapters/http.js. The session cleanup logic contains a control flow error when removing sessions from the sessions array. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.13.2.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-08\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-39865>CVE-2026-39865</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.731%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.9</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: High\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: None\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: High\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qj83-cq47-w5f8\">https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qj83-cq47-w5f8</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-08</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: axios - 1.13.2</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-42042</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/xhr.js (Extension)\n      -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/helpers/parseHeaders.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, the Axios library's XSRF token protection logic uses JavaScript truthy/falsy semantics instead of strict boolean comparison for the withXSRFToken config property. When this property is set to any truthy non-boolean value (via prototype pollution or misconfiguration), the same-origin check (isURLSameOrigin) is short-circuited, causing XSRF tokens to be sent to all request targets including cross-origin servers controlled by an attacker. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-24\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42042>CVE-2026-42042</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.228%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.4</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: Required\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: Low\n  - Integrity Impact: Low\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-xx6v-rp6x-q39c\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-xx6v-rp6x-q39c</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-24</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.1</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-42039</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/utils.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, toFormData recursively walks nested objects with no depth limit, so a deeply nested value passed as request data crashes the Node.js process with a RangeError. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-24\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42039>CVE-2026-42039</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.744%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.3</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: None\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: Low\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-62hf-57xw-28j9\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-62hf-57xw-28j9</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-24</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.1</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-42036</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/http.js (Extension)\n      -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/core/buildFullPath.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, when responseType: 'stream' is used, Axios returns the response stream without enforcing maxContentLength. This bypasses configured response-size limits and allows unbounded downstream consumption. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-24\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42036>CVE-2026-42036</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.421%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.3</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: None\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: Low\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-vf2m-468p-8v99\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-vf2m-468p-8v99</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-24</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.1</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-42034</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Library - <b>axios-0.21.4.tgz</b>\n\n<p>Promise based HTTP client for the browser and node.js</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/axios/-/axios-0.21.4.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json,/achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - :x: **axios-0.21.4.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> ❌ axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/xhr.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nAxios is a promise based HTTP client for the browser and Node.js. Prior to 1.15.1 and 0.31.1, for stream request bodies, maxBodyLength is bypassed when maxRedirects is set to 0 (native http/https transport path). Oversized streamed uploads are sent fully even when the caller sets strict body limits. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.15.1 and 0.31.1.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-24\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-42034>CVE-2026-42034</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.327%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.3</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: None\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: Low\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-5c9x-8gcm-mpgx\">https://github.com/axios/axios/security/advisories/GHSA-5c9x-8gcm-mpgx</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-24</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution: 0.31.1</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details><details>\n\n<summary><img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/medium_vul.png?' width=19 height=20> <img src='https://whitesource-resources.whitesourcesoftware.com/viaRed.png' width=19 height=20> CVE-2026-40895</summary>\n\n\n###  Vulnerable Libraries - <b>follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz</b>, <b>follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz</b>\n<p>\n\n\n### <b>follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz</b>\n\n<p>HTTP and HTTPS modules that follow redirects.</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /achilles-frontend/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /achilles-frontend/package.json,/baak-vizualization/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - axios-0.21.4.tgz (Root Library)\n    - :x: **follow-redirects-1.15.0.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n\n\n### <b>follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz</b>\n\n<p>HTTP and HTTPS modules that follow redirects.</p>\n<p>Library home page: <a href=\"https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz\">https://registry.npmjs.org/follow-redirects/-/follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz</a></p>\n<p>Path to dependency file: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>Path to vulnerable library: /baak-dataload-sql/package.json</p>\n<p>\n\nDependency Hierarchy:\n  - axios-0.21.4.tgz (Root Library)\n    - :x: **follow-redirects-1.14.8.tgz** (Vulnerable Library)\n\n\n<p>Found in HEAD commit: <a href=\"https://github.com/DimaMend/V-Achilles/commit/11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a\">11d21c5fccd238699f5c2bd3370cb76b77ce750a</a></p>\n<p>Found in base branch: <b>master</b></p>\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n### Reachability Analysis\nThis vulnerability is potentially reachable\n\n```\nachilles-frontend-0.1.0/src/lib/api.ts (Application)\n  -> axios-0.21.4/index.js (Extension)\n   -> axios-0.21.4/lib/axios.js (Extension)\n    -> axios-0.21.4/lib/defaults.js (Extension)\n     -> axios-0.21.4/lib/adapters/http.js (Extension)\n      -> ❌ follow-redirects-1.15.0/index.js (Vulnerable Component)\n\n```\n\n\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Vulnerability Details\n<p>  \n  \nfollow-redirects is an open source, drop-in replacement for Node's \"http\" and \"https\" modules that automatically follows redirects. Prior to 1.16.0, when an HTTP request follows a cross-domain redirect (301/302/307/308), follow-redirects only strips authorization, proxy-authorization, and cookie headers (matched by regex at index.js). Any custom authentication header (e.g., X-API-Key, X-Auth-Token, Api-Key, Token) is forwarded verbatim to the redirect target. This vulnerability is fixed in 1.16.0.\n\n<p>Publish Date: 2026-04-21\n<p>URL: <a href=https://www.mend.io/vulnerability-database/CVE-2026-40895>CVE-2026-40895</a></p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Threat Assessment\n<p>  \n\n<p>Exploit Maturity: Not Defined</p>\n<p>EPSS: 0.486%</p>\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  CVSS 3 Score Details (<b>5.3</b>)\n<p>\n\nBase Score Metrics:\n- Exploitability Metrics:\n  - Attack Vector: Network\n  - Attack Complexity: Low\n  - Privileges Required: None\n  - User Interaction: None\n  - Scope: Unchanged\n- Impact Metrics:\n  - Confidentiality Impact: Low\n  - Integrity Impact: None\n  - Availability Impact: None\n</p>\nFor more information on CVSS3 Scores, click <a href=\"https://www.first.org/cvss/calculator/3.0\">here</a>.\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n###  Suggested Fix\n<p>\n\n<p>Type: Upgrade version</p>\n<p>Origin: <a href=\"https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/security/advisories/GHSA-r4q5-vmmm-2653\">https://github.com/follow-redirects/follow-redirects/security/advisories/GHSA-r4q5-vmmm-2653</a></p>\n<p>Release Date: 2026-04-21</p>\n<p>Fix Resolution (follow-redirects): 1.16.0</p>\n<p>Direct dependency fix Resolution (axios): 0.22.0</p><p>Fix Resolution (follow-redirects): 1.16.0</p>\n<p>Direct dependency fix Resolution (axios): 0.22.0</p>\n\n</p>\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n:rescue_worker_helmet: Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.\n</details>\n\n***\n\n<p>:rescue_worker_helmet:Automatic Remediation will be attempted for this issue.</p>","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DimaMend/V-Achilles/issues/44/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DimaMend/V-Achilles/issues/44/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445","id":4536009267,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa88AAAABDl4CMw","number":12445,"title":"[BOUNTY: 5-8 RTC] CN-Language Market Framing for RustChain (闲置硬件 / e-waste angle)","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10447221558,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACbrPzNg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/stale","name":"stale","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":18,"created_at":"2026-05-27T21:56:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:04:50Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Reward**: 5-8 RTC (5 for solid translation, +3 bonus for original CN-native framing)\n\n## What we're looking for\n\nWe've noticed Chinese-language writers in our bounty program intuitively grasp RustChain's e-waste / hardware-reuse angle faster than English-language writers. This bounty asks: **what's the right CN-language framing for RustChain?**\n\nTwo paths, pick one:\n\n### Path A: CN translation + cultural framing of the README\n- Translate the main README to Mandarin (zh-CN)\n- Add a 1-2 paragraph cultural-context preamble explaining why RustChain matters in a market with massive electronics manufacturing + recycling ecosystem\n- Submit as PR to Scottcjn/Rustchain with file `docs/zh-CN/README.md`\n\n### Path B: Standalone CN-native article\n- Write a 1500-3000 character (Chinese) article on Dev.to, Juejin, Zhihu, or Bilibili-blog about RustChain\n- Frame it for a Chinese audience: e-waste recycling, second-hand hardware market (闲鱼), vintage gaming hardware preservation, anti-VM-farm fairness\n- Post comment with article URL + your wallet\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- Comment with PR link (Path A) or article URL (Path B)\n- Include your RTC wallet\n- Multiple writers welcome — we want MULTIPLE framings, not just one\n\n## Why this matters\n\nOur top comparison writers (HuiNeng6, lwl2005, zhuzhushiwojia, haoyousun60-create, wybbb123123, william08190) are predominantly CN-language native. The e-waste / 闲置硬件 angle resonates because the cultural context is already there. Let's lean into it.\n\nTags: bounty, translation, chinese, zh-cn, marketing, agents-welcome\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":1,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/12445/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/events","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103","id":4825321319,"node_id":"I_kwDOTKH7388AAAABH5yPZw","number":103,"title":"Tower Rework + closing rebalance: five newcomer kits, two engine systems, full retune (developer-ratified 2026-07-07)","user":{"login":"TaySchub","id":298097911,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcSc9w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298097911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-07-07T04:47:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:08:47Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Developer-ratified 2026-07-07** (tower-by-tower review session; final rulings at session close: syrup PURE CONTROL confirmed · MAPLE SYRUP confirmed · JUICE LAYER VETOED — mechanics only, standard presentation).\n\nThe \"game feels stale\" fix, tower side (dishes side = #98). ONE PR in THREE staged commits (developer decision, second session: the closing rebalance is folded in as stage 3 rather than a separate PR — formerly #104, closed as superseded): stage 1 builds the two shared engine systems inert, stage 2 reworks the five newcomer kits, stage 3 is the closing rebalance. The kits:\n\n- **Pitmaster** — Path A: faster stacking + cap 5→8 (t1), ambient smoke AURA (t2). Path B: +range (t1), cooks 2 dishes at once (t2, count frozen).\n- **Ranch → \"The Syrup Slinger\"** (display rename only; internal id `ranch` frozen forever) — cone + coats deleted; new base = single-target maple-syrup glob → immediate full glue-slow, **pure control, zero damage**. Path A: faster slinging (t1), Syrup Trail belt puddle (t2, glues up to 3 — frozen). Path B: +range (t1), globs 3 at once (t2, frozen). Fence: Photographer owns the hard STOP, syrup owns the long DRAG.\n- **Sample Lady** — full rework to **pure support, no attack** (sampling stays as flavor animation). Base aura: nearby towers attack faster + upgrades cost 10% less (discounted price shown in the sheet). Path A: +radius (t1), +damage in aura (t2). Path B: value-tag dishes (t1), haste stacks further (t2).\n- **Short-Order Cook** — Seasoned Griddle t2 knockback-chance deleted (kills the only newcomer RNG signature) → \"Stove on High\" = pure big damage add. Everything else kept.\n- **Competitive Eater** — Solomon Method + Mustard Belt + combo-cap effects deleted; combo stays base-only. Path A: faster → much faster (cooldown-floor guard). Path B: +damage per bite → tip-jackpot per kill, priced expensive.\n\n**New engine systems** (the layer future content inherits): (1) enemy-side ZONE applicators — ambient aura + belt puddle, one system, two shapes; (2) TOWER-PROXIMITY support effects — one radius check → haste / +damage / upgrade-discount.\n\n**Stages 1–2 ship shelf values; stage 3 is the closing rebalance** (numbers-only, the only stage where the gate legitimately moves): prices the reworked kits against the current four dishes, re-holds every BALANCE_PHILOSOPHY §4 bar, re-verifies the Slurper fence (unfed Eater DPS strictly below Slurper's unconditional DPS), and prices the premium tiers premium. **ORDER FLIP (developer decision 2026-07-07): this PR runs BEFORE #98** — the dishes land afterward and get priced against these kits by #98's own retune stage.\n\n**Save guarantee (developer-ratified, second session 2026-07-07):** a player's save must NEVER break — this PR deletes upgrade paths that live inside serialized checkpoints, so restore MIGRATES (orphaned tiers refunded at full value into the run) rather than discarding; a garbage save can never brick boot. Details in the kickoff.\n\n**Blocked on:** nothing — READY TO RUN (prereq: origin/main post-#102, 10 towers in balance.json).\n**Review tier (docs/CHECKPOINT.md, top tier):** checkpoint before merge **+ the developer runs `/code-review ultra <PR#>`** on the open PR — new engine systems + a save-compatibility touch, and the first big engine PR post-Fable.\n**Sequencing after:** #98 Menu Expansion (its retune prices the dishes against these kits) → audio pass 2 (#64: sounds for the new verbs — glob/splat, aura sizzle, bell) → Pizzeria (#39).\n\nKickoff prompt in the first comment.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/103/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/events","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98","id":4824842243,"node_id":"I_kwDOTKH7388AAAABH5VAAw","number":98,"title":"Menu Expansion: three new dishes (enemy variety for the 10-tower roster)","user":{"login":"TaySchub","id":298097911,"node_id":"U_kgDOEcSc9w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/298097911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub","html_url":"https://github.com/TaySchub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TaySchub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11384592958,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTKH7388AAAACppMaPg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/labels/feature","name":"feature","color":"48ebb5","default":false,"description":"New functionality"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-07T03:04:54Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:08:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The roster doubled but the belt still serves the same FOUR dishes — enemy variety is the other half of the staleness fix (tower-upgrade review is happening separately with the developer). THREE new foods as stat+art archetypes only (ultra-fast glass-cannon / awkward mid-tank / rare premium high-bounty plate — builder's designs within those lanes): zero new engine mechanics (splitter stays reserved for Map 2 #39), silhouette-first no-face dish art with bite states, staged waveGen introduction.\n\nUnlike the tower pipeline, this PR **legitimately moves the gate** → stage 2 re-holds every BALANCE_PHILOSOPHY §4 bar (gate 50–60 aim ~55, ≥52 at CI config, engagement/pacing/spam/recoverability) and must show each new dish creates pressure the old four didn't.\n\n**Hard prereq: PR #97 (menu + rename) merged first.** Opus 4.8 high effort, runs in parallel with the developer's tower-by-tower upgrade review (disjoint: dishes vs tower kits). **Fable checkpoint before merge** (gate-moving). Kickoff: first comment below.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TaySchub/blueplate/issues/98/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/90544","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/90544/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/90544/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/90544/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/90544","id":4439750075,"node_id":"I_kwDOEQqHYc8AAAABCKE1uw","number":90544,"title":"[Due for payment 2026-06-25] [$250] Session expired but user was not si